WEBVTT

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.640
Good morning,

00:00:13.890 --> 00:00:14.720
Hana!

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.430
- Good morning, Tama.
- Morning!

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.850
You're cheerful this morning, Tama.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.520
And you're lethargic this morning, Eiko!

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:26.440
When I think that our regular classes
start next week...

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.820
But the sports test is on Wednesday!

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.700
Sports test...

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:33.820
You don't like exercising?

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.660
Not really.

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:39.990
I love to move around,
so I'm looking forward to the sports test!

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.960
Tama, it seems
like you're always moving around.

00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:45.880
You make it sound like I'm sketchy!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.630
But my guess is you're good at athletics.

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.130
Nah, just average.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.760
For example, I got a B
for the sports test last year.

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.470
Oh, really?

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.550
I got a B, too.

00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:59.970
You're fast, right, Kamu?

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:01.850
Yeah, I am fast.

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:05.480
But when it comes to long-distance,
I run out of energy.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:08.820
So my results in last year's sports test
were in the mid-range, too.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.940
Then you're average
like the rest of us, Kamu!

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.440
<i>Last year...</i>

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:14.740
How did you do, Hana?

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:17.280
I think I got a B, too.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.620
Then we're the Four Mediocre-teers!

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:22.370
Mediocre-teers?

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:25.620
<i>I can't tell them I was just studying
for the high school exam last year.</i>

00:01:22.910 --> 00:01:24.500
Mediocre-teers?

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:00.760
EXAMINATION ROOM

00:02:57.550 --> 00:03:00.760
ONE YEAR AGO

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:00.760
Doctor, what is it?

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.430
Well...

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.180
She has the mumps.

00:03:08.440 --> 00:03:09.810
- The mumps...
- Oh!

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.150
I guess you didn't have them
as a child, did you, Hana?

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.650
I'll have to examine her first,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:18.700
but she'll have to stay home
from school for a while.

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:22.450
That's the mumps for you.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.240
If you get them as a teen or adult,
they can be a real pain.

00:03:27.330 --> 00:03:29.910
It's contagious, so for at least a week...

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.290
Um, I...

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.710
I have my high school
entrance exam tomorrow!

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:39.010
Well, that's...

00:03:39.550 --> 00:03:41.470
You'll just have to miss it.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.890
<i>From the following day, I had a high fever.</i>

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:51.900
<i>I don't remember much after that.</i>

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:56.900
GRADUATION CEREMONY

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:56.900
<i>After graduation, the period for taking
high school entrance exams was over.</i>

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:59.530
<i>I had totally recovered,</i>

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.660
<i>as if the mumps were waiting for that day.</i>

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.200
First your cheeks,
and now your eyes are gonna swell up.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.500
After all,

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:12.170
I don't know what to do!

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:16.500
Everyone else is going on to high school,
while I'm stuck in limbo!

00:04:16.710 --> 00:04:20.010
Look on the bright side
and use this time productively.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:23.090
Not many people can say
they were in high school limbo.

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.800
I don't wanna be able to say that either!

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.390
When you introduce yourself,

00:04:27.760 --> 00:04:29.640
you can say, "I'm a wandering student!"

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:31.140
Try it!

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:33.730
I don't wanna make light
of my situation like that!

00:04:34.020 --> 00:04:36.770
I don't want to go to school next year either.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.730
I don't even want to go outside.

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:40.740
Don't be silly.

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:45.320
But next year, my friends will be
a year ahead of me,

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:48.700
and I'll be a year behind them.

00:04:49.240 --> 00:04:52.710
My classmates will all be
a year younger than me! I'll be the oldest!

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:54.830
Who cares who's older or younger?

00:04:55.170 --> 00:04:57.710
I won't even be able to make friends.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:01.800
Anyway, I don't wanna go to school
or go outside!

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.510
I'm gonna be a shut-in!

00:05:05.260 --> 00:05:07.970
Hana, do you remember Shion?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.470
She's graduating from college this year.

00:05:11.730 --> 00:05:13.940
She's the landlady
at your uncle's apartment building.

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:18.440
Hana, move to an apartment there.

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:23.110
You mean you don't want me here
as a shut-in?

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:24.650
That's not what I mean.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.200
If you're in an environment
where no one knows you,

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.080
you'll be able to get a fresh start, right?

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.700
You can study for high school
entrance exams one more time.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.420
Just think of it as getting
a bit of a late start. Okay?

00:05:38.500 --> 00:05:39.340
Okay.

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.140
Starting next week, you have
afternoon classes, too, don't you?

00:05:47.390 --> 00:05:49.180
Do you want me to start
making you lunch to take?

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:50.560
Would you?

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.020
Of course.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:53.770
I like doing that kind of thing.

00:05:54.310 --> 00:05:55.770
Shion...

00:05:56.310 --> 00:05:57.270
Hana,

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.400
do you have a favorite character?

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:02.320
Y-You don't have to make characters
out of my lunch!

00:06:02.900 --> 00:06:04.110
You'll see.

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:10.160
Hana...

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:12.290
HANA

00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:12.290
Your name means "flower" and "name," right?

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.950
That's how you write your name, right?

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:17.500
Yeah. People often misread it as "Kana."

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:19.790
That's too bad.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:24.170
If your name were "Kana,"
we could put it together with my name...

00:06:24.460 --> 00:06:26.050
<i>- One, two...
- One, two...</i>

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:28.220
<i>- Kanaetamae!
- Kanaetamae!</i>

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:32.430
...and burst onto the scene as "Kanaetamae,"
a charming comedy duo...

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:33.930
But with "Hana,"

00:06:34.350 --> 00:06:35.480
people wouldn't go "Haha!"

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.270
Just kidding, Hana!

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:43.820
T-Tama?

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.320
It's okay, Hana. Good girl, good girl.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:48.490
Come on.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:50.320
Break it up.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.450
Give Hana space to breathe.

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:54.950
<i>She called me "Hana"!</i>

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:56.580
Oh, sorry.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:58.790
We tend to get too casual sometimes.

00:06:59.080 --> 00:07:00.000
No.

00:07:00.330 --> 00:07:01.880
That's fine.

00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.750
In that case, make you a deal?
I'll call you "Hana,"

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:06.760
and you call me "Eiko," no "Miss" or anything.

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:10.340
Sure.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:15.100
Everyone's casual
as far as Eiko is concerned.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:19.270
<i>We haven't even been here a week
and everyone's casual?</i>

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.810
Thanks for waiting!

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:25.070
Sorry it took me so long.

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:29.570
The school store has various baked goods
that I couldn't decide what to get.

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:31.820
Hey, that's a hot tip!

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:35.200
Maybe I'll buy me
some baked goodies tomorrow!

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:38.790
Kamu, that's one huge lunch!

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.420
Kamuri, are you going to eat all of that?

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:43.670
I would have no problem with it.

00:07:44.380 --> 00:07:45.550
But...

00:07:46.050 --> 00:07:49.090
I'm a slow eater,
so I won't be able to finish it all.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.140
So if you'd like, help me work on it.

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:54.140
I feel bad for you.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.980
Did you make that yourself, Tama?

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:02.850
I'm impressed you could tell, Eiko.

00:08:03.100 --> 00:08:05.900
Actually, I'm in charge of cooking at home.

00:08:06.150 --> 00:08:07.780
Tama, that's great!

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.900
I wouldn't go that far.

00:08:11.360 --> 00:08:14.120
Hana, you live with your cousin, right?

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.080
Did she make lunch for you?

00:08:16.950 --> 00:08:17.740
Yeah.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.210
Your cousin is the landlady
of your apartment building, right?

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:22.580
Yeah.

00:08:22.830 --> 00:08:25.630
She's good at cooking
and always makes me dinner.

00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:28.250
A landlady who's good at cooking...

00:08:28.670 --> 00:08:30.630
That sounds like something
from a romance novel.

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:33.510
What kind of romantic lunch is it?

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:34.590
Good question!

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:37.560
Normal. It's a normal lunch.

00:08:40.430 --> 00:08:42.020
What is this lunch?

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:45.690
Are you dating your cousin?

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:49.110
N-No! I told you, Shion is a woman!

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:51.320
No problem!
You have our blessing!

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.320
She's a woman and I'm a woman!

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:55.950
What are you smiling about?

00:08:57.330 --> 00:08:58.950
Huh? What is that?

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:00.290
Soup.

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:03.330
My little sister gave it to me
so I'd get more nutritional balance.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.040
Your little sister is very kind.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:07.290
I'll call it...

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:09.920
"sis-sauce"!

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:13.380
"Sis-sauce"?
At least call it "sis-soup" or something.

00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:15.930
I don't know about that one, Hana.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:22.560
"Sis-sauce" sounds like it was made
from my sister's secretions,

00:09:22.850 --> 00:09:27.060
but "sis-soup" sounds
like my sister was actually cooked.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:29.520
Anyway, have a cup.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:30.780
All right.

00:09:33.900 --> 00:09:35.110
Sis-sauce is good!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:36.870
Have a sip, Hana!

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.660
O-Okay.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:42.370
Delicious!

00:09:42.620 --> 00:09:46.210
Even though we haven't met her yet,
it tastes like Eiko's little sister!

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:49.420
And now, to pay you back
for that tasty sis-sauce...

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:51.050
Here! Say "Aaah."

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:52.300
Aaah.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:57.140
Yummy!

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:58.760
That's our Tama!

00:09:59.050 --> 00:10:00.390
You have one, too, Hana!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:01.970
Th-Thank...

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:06.060
- So good!
- Right?

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.270
Tama, you're really good at cooking!

00:10:09.230 --> 00:10:11.110
You're making me blush!

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.030
This is heaven!

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:17.070
To be honest, I've always admired
Tama's homemade cooking.

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:20.330
During home ec in middle school,

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:24.950
the aroma coming from Tama's table
was always mouth-watering!

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:29.250
I thought then, "I hope I get a chance
to sample her cooking someday."

00:10:30.250 --> 00:10:32.170
You're making me feel bashful!

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:34.840
W-We are still talking about cooking, right?

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:39.680
But your little sister is really good
at cooking, too, Eiko!

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:41.930
How old is she?

00:10:42.310 --> 00:10:44.640
Fourteen.
She's a third-year middle school student.

00:10:44.970 --> 00:10:47.190
Then is she studying
for high school entrance exams?

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:49.440
That's right.

00:10:49.730 --> 00:10:52.360
She wants to go here, too.

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:55.360
Then "sis-sauce" will be "junior-sauce"!

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:56.860
Right, "junior-sauce."

00:10:57.700 --> 00:11:03.790
The thing is, she always studies late
but still makes sis-sauce every day.

00:11:04.290 --> 00:11:06.370
I'm worried that she'll get sick.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:07.790
And rightly so!

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.540
H-Hana?

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:15.920
It's awesome that she's working hard
to prepare for the entrance exams!

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.880
But for entrance exams,
first you need stamina!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:21.890
Still, you can't be healthy
and just call it a day!

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:25.100
Because you never know
what dangers are waiting for you!

00:11:25.930 --> 00:11:26.730
Huh?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.560
Get your sister to keep that in mind!

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:32.270
O-Okay.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.820
I'll pass that on.

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:37.190
S-Sorry.

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:41.910
No, we can tell that you feel strongly
about high school entrance exams.

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.620
Right, Kamu?

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:44.740
Kamuri?

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:50.540
Come to think of it,
she hasn't uttered a single word.

00:11:51.670 --> 00:11:54.420
Kamu is always silent when she's eating.

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.220
She's choking!

00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:01.430
K-Kamu!

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:02.340
Kamuri!

00:12:02.340 --> 00:12:04.720
Sis-sauce, sis-sauce!

00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:06.060
No, water!

00:12:11.140 --> 00:12:13.900
Shion, thank you for making me lunch.

00:12:15.070 --> 00:12:16.070
No problem.

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:17.690
Was it good?

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:19.440
Yeah, delicious.

00:12:19.940 --> 00:12:20.780
But...

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:23.030
I'm sorry!

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:26.370
I appreciate your feelings,
but I can't go out with you!

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:35.920
EXERCISE WEARS ME OUT

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:35.920
Isn't it great not having
any classes for one day?

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:38.710
They should do it once a week.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:40.550
The sports test...

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:45.180
Getting tested that much
would leave us exhausted!

00:12:45.430 --> 00:12:47.850
True. And they would learn all about us.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.770
You've got a dirty mind.

00:12:52.230 --> 00:12:55.520
<i>They said they weren't especially good
at athletics, right?</i>

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:58.070
<i>I'm not good at it, either.</i>

00:12:58.530 --> 00:13:02.150
<i>But maybe I won't stand out
if I'm with them.</i>

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:05.820
Let's go get some water!

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:07.280
I'm exhausted!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.430
Hana, are you okay?

00:13:25.720 --> 00:13:27.390
- Poop...
- Poop?

00:13:29.970 --> 00:13:31.220
Pooped...

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:32.520
out.

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:33.980
Oh, she's pooped out!

00:13:35.940 --> 00:13:39.320
Maybe it was a mistake
to start with the endurance run.

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.400
Eiko?

00:13:42.110 --> 00:13:45.030
When we were talking about the sports test
a couple days ago,

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:48.410
Hana said she was average, didn't she?

00:13:49.120 --> 00:13:53.290
If this is "average" for her,
then I'm curious about her "sub-par."

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.080
Oh, I see.

00:13:55.580 --> 00:13:57.210
You two are mean!

00:14:01.760 --> 00:14:06.380
<i>I actually was more or less average
back in middle school.</i>

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:10.430
What's wrong?

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:15.140
I haven't exercised
since middle school graduation,

00:14:15.140 --> 00:14:17.850
which is why I'm totally out of shape.

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.230
One month and you're out of shape?

00:14:21.070 --> 00:14:22.860
Good point! You're right!

00:14:26.450 --> 00:14:28.320
The softball toss is next.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:30.660
Can you stand up?

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:33.370
Y-Yeah. I'm fine.

00:14:34.540 --> 00:14:35.410
Kamuri?

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:36.620
Grab hold.

00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:39.580
Th-Thanks.

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:50.850
Fourteen meters!

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:52.560
That's farther than last year.

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:53.180
Next, Tokura.

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:00.400
Seven meters!

00:15:00.650 --> 00:15:01.900
Next, Ichinose.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:04.320
I've got good control, anyway.

00:15:07.110 --> 00:15:07.860
Ouch!

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:09.200
Right!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.210
Are you okay, Hana?

00:15:18.210 --> 00:15:19.170
Wow!

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:21.880
For being short, she's really fast!

00:15:33.140 --> 00:15:34.640
Hey, Sengoku!

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:37.480
That 50 meter you ran was awesome!

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:39.310
Wanna join the track and field club?

00:15:39.850 --> 00:15:41.600
You can even do it on a trial basis!

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:44.150
Or just start by sitting in once?

00:15:44.730 --> 00:15:46.610
You wouldn't have to prepare!

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:48.400
<i>Wow, Kamuri is being scouted
by the track and field club!</i>

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:48.400
Just come by and check us out!

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:51.530
You have athletic legs, Sengoku!

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:53.120
With you on board,

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.700
U-U-Um...

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.700
I could see us doing decently
even at the prefectural tournament!

00:15:55.410 --> 00:15:58.290
So, in middle school,
what club were you in?

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:59.410
E-Eiko...

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:00.170
I didn't know what club
I wanted to be in until—

00:16:00.170 --> 00:16:01.210
Okay!

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:03.750
Eiko...

00:16:04.250 --> 00:16:05.380
Sorry.

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.760
She's really shy.

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.760
I-I was just a little surprised.

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:13.970
S-Sorry for scaring you.

00:16:14.220 --> 00:16:15.720
Jeez, Amane!

00:16:16.100 --> 00:16:18.730
You'd scare anyone
with your aggressive come-on!

00:16:19.730 --> 00:16:20.600
Today...

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:23.440
you came for me, Eiko.

00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:34.450
Hana!

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:37.450
You did great! You tried so hard!

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.870
You've just got this to do.

00:16:40.120 --> 00:16:41.790
Th-Then it's over!

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:52.430
Um, right arm 26.

00:16:53.050 --> 00:16:53.970
That's average!

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:57.010
You did it! A normal score!

00:16:57.350 --> 00:16:58.310
Normal...

00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.930
Yes! Normal!

00:17:01.020 --> 00:17:03.520
<i>Normal! Thank goodness!</i>

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:06.270
<i>I got a brilliantly normal result,</i>

00:17:06.520 --> 00:17:09.780
<i>and now I'm done
with this torturous sports test!</i>

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:11.820
<i>My body feels light!</i>

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.870
M-My leg cramped up!

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:19.080
Hana?

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.750
What's the matter?
Are you all right?

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:23.540
I'll get a compress
from the infirmary!

00:17:23.790 --> 00:17:25.830
Th-Thank you, Tama.

00:17:26.330 --> 00:17:28.250
Don't worry about it!

00:17:28.750 --> 00:17:31.590
Tama, you're so kind!

00:17:32.840 --> 00:17:35.180
I discovered an ice cream vending machine!

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:36.680
H-Huh?

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:42.810
We've got an ice cream vending machine
on school grounds!

00:17:43.180 --> 00:17:45.270
Um... the compress...

00:17:45.270 --> 00:17:46.770
It's got strawberry cheesecake flavor?

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:47.860
Too fast!

00:17:48.110 --> 00:17:51.610
I mean, we get to eat ice cream at school!

00:17:51.990 --> 00:17:54.030
You two lack emotions!

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.990
At least come up with a haiku!

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:58.620
Owowowowow!

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:58.620
Again?

00:17:59.030 --> 00:18:00.830
It looks like this is a thing with her.

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:08.380
Well, my grandma told me that eating
a banana or kiwi is good for leg cramps.

00:18:08.790 --> 00:18:09.670
For leg cramps?

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.170
A banana?

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.590
They've got banana choco mint Hawaiian.

00:18:14.590 --> 00:18:15.380
That'll do it!

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.140
Here, eat it!

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:20.260
Go ahead!

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:26.020
How do you feel?

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.150
Cured?

00:18:29.560 --> 00:18:33.400
Tama, I don't think this is
what your grandmother had in mind.

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:34.190
Oh my!

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:36.150
And it's disgusting.

00:18:36.950 --> 00:18:37.820
Wow...

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:38.910
Teacher!

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.280
You found this already?

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.410
Jeez, are you guys ants?

00:18:44.660 --> 00:18:45.830
Ants...

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:47.250
What are you looking at?

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.920
I'm curious what flavor you're gonna get.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:52.500
Maybe rum raisin since you're an adult?

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:53.920
Now there are more of you!

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.130
What do you care what I get?

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:00.850
Lick!

00:19:02.600 --> 00:19:04.520
Finish that up, then go!

00:19:04.770 --> 00:19:05.850
Okay!

00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:11.190
She bought
banana chocolate mint Hawaiian, huh?

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.780
Maybe she has a leg cramp, too.

00:19:14.530 --> 00:19:17.360
Which reminds me,
do you feel okay now, Hana?

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:19.820
Yeah. I'm fine now.

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:23.160
That must be thanks to the banana effect!

00:19:23.450 --> 00:19:24.540
All right!

00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:26.500
The afternoon sports test!

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:28.580
Let's do our best!

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:30.130
There's more?

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:42.350
Jeez, Tama, you got me!

00:19:43.760 --> 00:19:45.560
It was actually only in the morning.

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:49.140
You're mean to me, Tama.

00:19:49.390 --> 00:19:52.310
- Kamu, that took you a long time.
- Sorry.

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:55.570
Kamu, you're not wearing socks?

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.690
We're just going home.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.700
No socks, I like it! That's fresh!

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:03.030
Why are you so excited about it?

00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:05.040
You don't get it?

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:07.540
A girl who usually wears tights
is bare-legged!

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:09.460
You've gotta appreciate the difference!

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:11.790
Sorry, I don't get it.

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:13.290
For example,

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:17.630
imagine I live in a nudist colony,
never wearing a stitch of clothing!

00:20:13.290 --> 00:20:20.380
NUDIST COLONY
BEAUTY PAGEANT

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:20.380
Then one day,
I show up in a school uniform!

00:20:20.680 --> 00:20:22.550
Doesn't that difference excite you?

00:20:23.140 --> 00:20:25.640
No, you just confused me even more.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:27.680
Hana, do you understand?

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:30.890
Why am I even asking?

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:35.150
So the idea of Tama naked
doesn't make her excited?

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:36.730
Is that what we were talking about?

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.780
Look, naked or bare-legged,
let's go home.

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:42.910
Bare-legged!

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.380
Is it good?

00:20:56.290 --> 00:20:57.590
You want another helping?

00:20:59.880 --> 00:21:02.760
Did anything fun happen at school?

00:21:03.220 --> 00:21:04.470
That's great!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:07.260
That reminds me.

00:21:07.510 --> 00:21:09.180
I need to make you lunch for tomorrow.

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:11.600
About that, Shion...

00:21:11.940 --> 00:21:12.980
Don't worry.

00:21:13.230 --> 00:21:15.940
I won't make it
so your friends get the wrong idea again.

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:17.770
Sorry, Shion.

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:19.360
It's fine!

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:22.990
You've been living here for a year,
so I know what a pain you are.

00:21:33.620 --> 00:21:37.290
She looks like a mechanical doll
carrying tea.

00:21:38.000 --> 00:21:39.050
That's elegant.

00:21:39.500 --> 00:21:42.050
I-I have pain in all my muscles.

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:43.380
Her whole body...

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:47.470
I-I got out of shape during spring vacation.

00:21:47.760 --> 00:21:52.270
What kind of lazy spring vacation
did you have to get so weak?

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:56.900
Okay, okay, but eat your loving cousin's
lunch and get energized!

00:21:57.360 --> 00:22:00.400
I told you, it's not like that with us!

00:22:03.530 --> 00:22:05.360
- Th-They broke up?
- Th-They broke up?

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:08.240
Sh-Shion!
